  "body": "## Why this change is needed\n\nNative source export was integrated in PR #7, but agents could not yet complete the adopted surface workflow through a versioned program service, and the complete M01–M12 release gate had no executable evidence audit.\n\n## What this delivers\n\n- Explicit `ontokin.agent/0.3` binding for source-authoritative `surface-0.1` programs and GLB/0.3, with separate durable stores and unchanged earlier defaults.\n- Profile-aware discovery, bounded summaries and revision-bound `surface.mesh_page` (at most 256 complete triangles), atomic native section/material repair, evaluation and exact artifact retrieval.\n- Final response-budget enforcement inside publication transactions, controlled startup failures, and preservation of stores with a mismatched schema.\n- Actual Agent/0.3 workflows for 22 source fixtures, ordinary/generated compositions, scoped repairs, rejected candidates and insertion/reorder/removal. Native geometry comes from `.ok` programs.\n- Executable M01–M12 mapping with strict source/artifact/browser/regression/CI identity checks, independent destination and visual checks, and additive CI.\n- Durable release archive, hash index, evidence summary, updated GOAL/STATUS and precise continuation task.\n\n## Verified results\n\nThe complete release gate passed on implementation `80d59bb2b09a5a57cad8e1b477d89f23a3e5a5a1` (runtime `abebb2fe7f5af46862db0c24a83c244113a2cfabea1b8a69a22260e4aef2d4d6`). All 182 eligible verification inputs are byte-identical in the archival head `3e7a2a61a68a7f7442cbe59e97753405ffbc7856`; exact Git-tree and inventory checks passed.\n\n- **464/464 tests**; 43 original source cases / 694 assertions; A01–A10; fresh current C01–C20 all passed.\n- **M01–M12: 12 passed, zero failed/pending**, with 61 actual mapped test methods.\n- 492 actual exchanges, 22 retrieved native GLBs; Khronos zero errors/warnings/infos/hints; geometry/winding/normals/PBR/placement and 308 independent Three.js poses passed.\n- Four browser fixtures, 84 pose comparisons and 12 individually reviewed captures; no page/console/network failures.\n- Exact implementation CI [39153863765](https://github.com/Omegapy/OntoKin/actions/runs/39153863765): Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 and GLB/visual jobs all passed. Archival-head CI runs separately before integration.\n- Independent review verified every one of the 1,247 archive entries against the frozen output and manifest. Archive SHA-256: `8c49bdeee3cadd5d80883b57937da3c13c815e7ea3ffe56e49efd3324bae761d`.\n- Documentation preservation: 29 historical sources, 233 sections and 602 local links passed.\n\nSee [retained evidence](docs/engineering/surface-release-validation/README.md) and [OK-ENG-004](docs/engineering/OK-ENG-004-native-surface-release-conformance.md) for complete identities, acceptance and reproduction. Issue #8 records ownership and checkpoints.\n\n## Scope and integration\n\nThis completes the named native surface gate; the full OntoKin goal remains in progress. Contacts, general dynamics, forces, controllers, textures/skinning, live destination behavior and other product domains remain open. Visual surfaces add no physical matter or motion authority. The next task is a separately specified source impulse profile with off-center angular response and predetermined acceptance fixtures.\n\nRoot owns the bounded main integration lease. Merge uses the observed main head without force, preserves concurrent history, and is followed by independent inspection of resulting-main CI. The owner-disabled automation remains unchanged.",
